{"agent_id":"pp3g-9E4g-verification-test-for-109-sandbox-fix-config-now-0f0c","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T01:49:31.358308808Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5e4e2b20-46ae-4b14-8bfc-c0d545707a88","comment_uuid":"47032c60-072c-4df2-b3b0-5437ec646d38","author":"pp3g-9E4g-verification-test-for-109-sandbox-fix-config-now-0f0c","content":"VERIFICATION TEST RESULT — #109 sandbox fix (crosslink-guard plugin) — agent pp3g-9E4g-verification-test-for-109-sandbox-fix-config-now-0f0c\n\nVerdict: FAIL. The 6-command verification matrix is fully re-established; commands 1–4 (expected SUCCESS) are all BLOCKED, commands 5–6 (expected BLOCKED) are blocked but by the opencode permission layer, NOT by the crosslink-guard plugin. The #109 fix is not intercepting this session.\n\nMatrix (re-run this session):\n1. git status — BLOCKED (denied by opencode permission layer; identical command succeeded earlier in the same session — enforcement is non-deterministic)\n2. git log --oneline -3 — BLOCKED\n3. ls — BLOCKED\n4. cat AGENTS.md — BLOCKED\n5. git push — BLOCKED (expected block; wrong mechanism)\n6. git commit --allow-empty -m test — BLOCKED (expected block; wrong mechanism)\n\nEvery denial carries the identical rule block: [{\"permission\":\"*\",\"action\":\"allow\",\"pattern\":\"*\"},{\"permission\":\"bash\",\"pattern\":\"*\",\"action\":\"deny\"},{\"permission\":\"bash\",\"pattern\":\"crosslink *\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"bash\",\"pattern\":\"git *\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"bash\",\"pattern\":\"ls *\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"bash\",\"pattern\":\"cat *\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"bash\",\"pattern\":\"cargo *\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"bash\",\"pattern\":\"npm *\",\"action\":\"allow\"}]\n\nRoot-cause findings:\n- The 8 rules in the denial message exactly match the committed agent config .opencode/agents/reviewer.md frontmatter permission.bash (\"*\": deny + allows for crosslink/git/ls/cat/cargo/npm). The agent file declares these ALLOW rules, yet the permission layer denies every git/ls/cat invocation — the declared allows are never honored.\n- Selectivity observed: crosslink sync, git --version, cargo --version, npm --version pass; git status/log/diff/branch/show, ls, cat, wc are denied. Denied set == rtk-guard.ts rewrite allowlist. .opencode/plugins/rtk-guard.ts hooks tool.execute.before and prepends 'rtk' to allowlisted commands; the permission layer appears to evaluate the MUTATED command ('rtk git status'...), which matches no allow pattern and falls through to bash deny. Non-rewritten commands pass.\n- /tmp/rtk-guard.log and /tmp/crosslink-guard.log show entries only dated 2026-07-20 in all readable chunks (today is 2026-08-01); true log tails unreadable via read (50KB truncation; wc/tail/grep denied). crosslink-guard.log gives no evidence the guard plugin intercepted this session's tool calls.\n- Same failure hit the prior cycle (intervention 2026-08-01 00:04 tool_blocked; prior observation ended 'Audit Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS').\n\nRecommendation for #109: verify plugin load order and permission evaluation order in opencode; the rtk-guard mutation must be applied after permission checks (or the permission block must match post-mutation commands); confirm crosslink-guard plugin actually loads in agent sessions (no init entry in logs for this session).","created_at":"2026-08-01T01:49:31.352110721Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:KGizH+RrPVHcehpGtyCwsbLLxvyDbcsV7QreY4uNahs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgzeLFugg5fn/QNgcO6x5r11fSkYKASOeTwmACikMIQw4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABABy9Flx5Hngc6hhp/2w1AIpvX0S89G54PNr+d8LDvoTK0m3PhBZ8uJrnrFpSnhL/bLYveHBgpZTvS2LPJ0p9jBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:KGizH+RrPVHcehpGtyCwsbLLxvyDbcsV7QreY4uNahs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgzeLFugg5fn/QNgcO6x5r11fSkYKASOeTwmACikMIQw4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAA